1
00:00:57,580 --> 00:01:00,140
ALARM CLOCK BUZZES

2
00:01:09,540 --> 00:01:12,293
Bye. See you later.

3
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:04,216
'This is a customer announcement.
The store closes in five minutes.'

4
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:10,571
Oi!

5
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:40,579
Wilson?

6
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:44,130
I've got the lottery money.

7
00:02:44,220 --> 00:02:46,415
Wilson?

8
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:48,536
You there?

9
00:02:50,060 --> 00:02:54,190
I can't hang about
cos they're closing the shop.

10
00:02:54,100 --> 00:02:56,110
Wilson?

11
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,853
(Oh, come on.)

12
00:02:58,940 --> 00:03:02,216
SOMETHING BANGS
Hello?

13
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:07,659
Hello? Wilson, it's Rose.

14
00:03:09,620 --> 00:03:11,929
Hello?

15
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:14,932
W... Wilson?

16
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:41,735
Wilson!

17
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:52,130
Wilson?

18
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:58,969
DOOR SLAMS SHUT

19
00:04:07,140 --> 00:04:10,180
(Oh, you're kidding me!)

20
00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:12,455
SOMETHING BANGS

21
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:18,376
Is that someone mucking about?

22
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:29,974
Who is it?

23
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:48,375
OK. You got me. Very funny.

24
00:04:51,540 --> 00:04:56,978
Right, I've got the joke!
Whose idea was this? Is it Derek's?

25
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:59,574
Is it?

26
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:02,128
Derek, is this you?

27
00:05:24,580 --> 00:05:26,377
Run!

28
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:58,540
You pulled his arm off!
Yep, plastic.

29
00:05:58,140 --> 00:06:02,213
Very clever, nice trick. Who are
they, students? A student thing?

30
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:04,609
Why would they be students?
I don't know!

31
00:06:04,700 --> 00:06:06,338
You said it. Why students?

32
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:10,618
Cos... that many people dressed up
and being silly has to be students.

33
00:06:10,700 --> 00:06:15,251
That makes sense. Well done.
Thanks. They're not students.

34
00:06:15,340 --> 00:06:20,858
When Wilson finds them, he'll call the police.
- Who's Wilson?
- Chief electrician.
- Wilson's dead.

35
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:23,657
That's just not funny. That's sick!

36
00:06:23,740 --> 00:06:26,300
Mind your eyes.
I've had enough of this.

37
00:06:26,380 --> 00:06:30,293
Who are you, then?
Who's that lot down there...?

38
00:06:30,380 --> 00:06:32,336
I said WHO are they?

39
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:34,536
They're living plastic creatures.

40
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:39,410
They're being controlled
by a relay device from the roof,
which would be a great big problem

41
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:43,493
IF I didn't have this. So I'm gonna
go upstairs and blow it up.

42
00:06:43,580 --> 00:06:45,571
I might well die, but don't worry(!)

43
00:06:45,660 --> 00:06:49,289
You go home. Go and have
your lovely beans on toast.

44
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:53,890
Don't tell anyone.
If you do, you'll get them killed.

45
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:57,568
I'm the Doctor, what's your name?
Rose.

46
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,855
Nice to meet you. Run for your life!

47
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:57,971
TV: 'Central London has been closed
off as police investigate the fire.'

48
00:07:58,060 --> 00:08:02,258
I know, it's on the telly! It's
everywhere, she's lucky to be alive.

49
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:05,457
Honestly, it's aged her.
Skin like an old Bible.

50
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:07,656
You'd think I was her daughter.

51
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:12,180
Oh, and here's himself. I've been
phoning! You could have been dead!

52
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:14,694
It's all on the news!
I can't believe your shop went up!

53
00:08:14,780 --> 00:08:17,419
Honestly, I'm fine. Don't fuss!

54
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:19,456
But what happened? I don't know.

55
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:23,579
What caused it? I wasn't in there. I
was outside, I didn't see anything.

56
00:08:23,660 --> 00:08:27,653
It's Debbie. She knows a man on the
Mirror, 500 quid for an interview.

57
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:29,810
Oh, that's brilliant, give it here.

58
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:35,934
You've got to find some way to make
money. I'm not bailing you out.

59
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:38,110
PHONE RINGS

60
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:39,931
Bev, she's alive!

61
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:43,217
I've told her,
sue for compensation...

62
00:08:43,300 --> 00:08:47,293
She was within seconds of death.
You drinking tea? That's no good!

63
00:08:47,380 --> 00:08:49,177
You need something stronger. I'm OK.

64
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:52,889
You deserve a proper drink.
We're going down the pub. My treat.

65
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:56,893
Is there a match on? ...No, no...
I'm just thinking about you!

66
00:08:56,980 --> 00:09:01,496
There's a match on, ain't there? We
COULD catch the last five minutes.

67
00:09:01,580 --> 00:09:03,536
Go on, then. I'm fine, really, go.

68
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:05,611
And get rid of that.

69
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:17,656
Bye-bye. Bye! Aaaggghhh!

70
00:09:17,740 --> 00:09:22,256
'15 fire crews are present, though
it's thought there's little chance

71
00:09:22,340 --> 00:09:25,130
'of saving the infrastructure.'

72
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:46,375
ALARM CLOCK BUZZES

73
00:09:51,940 --> 00:09:58,175
There's no point in getting up,
sweetheart. You've no job to go to.

74
00:10:01,820 --> 00:10:04,380
There's Finch's. You could try them.

75
00:10:04,460 --> 00:10:08,169
They've always got jobs.
Oh, great, the butcher's.

76
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:11,138
It might be good.
You were getting airs and graces.

77
00:10:11,220 --> 00:10:15,452
I'm not joking about compensation,
you've had genuine shock and trauma.

78
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:21,331
Arianna got 2,000 quid off the
council, just cos the old man behind
the desk said she looked Greek!

79
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:25,413
I know she is Greek, but that's
not the point. It was a valid claim.

80
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:33,533
Mum, you're such a liar! I said to
nail the cat-flap. We'll get strays!

81
00:10:33,620 --> 00:10:36,930
I did it weeks back.
Na... you thought about it.

82
00:10:52,860 --> 00:10:57,376
What are you doing here? I live here.
What do you do that for? Cos I do!

83
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:59,530
I'm here cos someone blew up my job!

84
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:04,899
I must have the wrong signal.
You're not plastic, are you?
Nope, bonehead. Bye.

85
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:06,652
You, inside, right now.

86
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:08,651
Who is it?

87
00:11:08,740 --> 00:11:11,777
It's about last night.
He's part of the inquiry.

88
00:11:11,860 --> 00:11:14,579
She deserves compensation!

89
00:11:14,660 --> 00:11:17,174
Oh, we're talking millions.

90
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:20,172
I'm... I'm in my dressing gown.

91
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:22,854
Yes, you are.

92
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:26,250
There's a strange man in my bedroom.

93
00:11:26,340 --> 00:11:31,209
Yes, there is.
..Well, anything could happen.

94
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:34,770
No.

95
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:39,580
Don't mind the mess. Coffee?

96
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:42,150
Might as well, thanks, just milk.

97
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:43,852
We should go to the police.

98
00:11:43,940 --> 00:11:47,250
Seriously. That won't last.
He's gay and she's an alien.

99
00:11:47,340 --> 00:11:51,458
I'm not blaming you, even if it was
some sort of joke... Sad ending.

100
00:11:51,540 --> 00:11:55,852
It said on the news
they found a body. "Rose Tyler."

101
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:59,932
Ah, could've been worse.
Look at the ears!

102
00:12:00,020 --> 00:12:03,296
He was nice. He was a nice bloke.

103
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:07,931
Anyway, if we do go to the police,
I wanna know what I'm saying.

104
00:12:08,020 --> 00:12:10,454
I want you to explain. Maybe not.

105
00:12:10,540 --> 00:12:14,135
FLAPPING SOUND
What's that? ...Have you got a cat?

106
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:21,171
No. We did have, but we just get
strays. They come in off the estate.

107
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:28,851
I told Mickey to chuck that out.

108
00:12:28,940 --> 00:12:31,898
You're all the same.
Give a man a plastic hand...

109
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:35,495
Anyway, I don't even know your name.
Doctor what?

110
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:08,940
It's all right, I've stopped it.
There. See... armless! You think?!

111
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:12,818
Hold on a minute,
you can't just go swanning off?

112
00:13:12,900 --> 00:13:14,856
I can. This is me, swanning off.

113
00:13:14,940 --> 00:13:20,140
But that arm was moving,
it tried to kill me! Well observed.
You can't walk away!

114
00:13:20,100 --> 00:13:24,130
That's not fair. You've got to tell
me what's going on. No, I don't.

115
00:13:26,220 --> 00:13:30,179
All right, I'll go to the police.
I'll tell everyone.

116
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:36,449
You said I'd get people killed, so,
your choice. Tell me or I'll talk.

117
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:39,532
Is that supposed to sound tough?
Sort of.

118
00:13:39,620 --> 00:13:43,533
Doesn't work. Who are you?
Told you, the Doctor.

119
00:13:43,620 --> 00:13:45,611
Yeah, but Doctor what?

120
00:13:45,700 --> 00:13:48,339
Just the Doctor. The Doctor? Hello!

121
00:13:48,420 --> 00:13:51,571
Is that meant to sound impressive?!

122
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,571
Sort of.

123
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:58,170
Come on then, you can tell me.
I've seen enough.

124
00:13:58,100 --> 00:14:02,571
Are you the police? No! I was just
passing. I'm a long way from home...

125
00:14:02,660 --> 00:14:06,573
But what have I done wrong? How come
those plastic things come after me?

126
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:10,494
Oh, suddenly the entire world
revolves around you.

127
00:14:10,580 --> 00:14:12,536
You got in the way, that's all.

128
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:15,578
It tried to kill me!
It was after me, not you!

129
00:14:15,660 --> 00:14:19,335
I was in the shop, you blundered in,
almost ruined it all!

130
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:24,858
I was tracking it down, it was
tracking me down. It fixed on you
cos you'd met me.

131
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:28,728
So, you're saying the entire world
revolves around you?

132
00:14:28,820 --> 00:14:30,776
Sort of, yeah. You're full of it!

133
00:14:30,860 --> 00:14:32,657
Sort of, yeah.

134
00:14:32,740 --> 00:14:36,653
All this plastic stuff,
who else knows? No-one.

135
00:14:36,740 --> 00:14:38,696
What, you're on your own?

136
00:14:38,780 --> 00:14:42,739
Well, who else is there? I mean, you
lot, all you do is eat chips, sleep

137
00:14:42,820 --> 00:14:47,291
and watch telly while underneath you,
there's a war going on.

138
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:50,133
OK. Start from the beginning.

139
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:56,451
I mean, if we're going with living
plastic, and I don't believe that,

140
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:58,895
how did you kill it?

141
00:14:58,980 --> 00:15:02,939
The thing controlling it projects
life into it. I cut off the signal.

142
00:15:03,020 --> 00:15:06,251
So, radio control? Thought control.

143
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,331
You all right? Yeah.

144
00:15:08,420 --> 00:15:10,331
So... who's controlling it, then?

145
00:15:10,420 --> 00:15:14,936
Long story. What's it all for? Shop
window dummies, what's that about?

146
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:18,933
Is someone trying to take over
Britain's shops?!

147
00:15:19,020 --> 00:15:21,136
No!

148
00:15:21,220 --> 00:15:23,654
Well, no! It's not a price war.

149
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:28,814
They want to overthrow the human race
and destroy you.

150
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:31,160
Do you believe me? No.

151
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:33,250
But you're still listening.

152
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:36,569
Really, though, Doctor... Tell me.

153
00:15:36,660 --> 00:15:38,696
Who are you?

154
00:15:41,940 --> 00:15:46,920
Do you know like we were saying?
About the Earth revolving?

155
00:15:47,740 --> 00:15:49,935
It's like when you're a kid.

156
00:15:50,020 --> 00:15:53,774
The first time they tell you
the world's turning

157
00:15:53,860 --> 00:15:58,536
and you can't believe it cos it looks
like everything's standing still.

158
00:15:58,620 --> 00:16:01,134
..I can feel it.

159
00:16:03,340 --> 00:16:05,331
The turn of the Earth.

160
00:16:05,420 --> 00:16:09,174
The ground beneath our feet
is spinning at 1, 000 miles an hour.

161
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:13,139
The entire planet is hurtling round
the sun at 67, 000 miles an hour.

162
00:16:13,220 --> 00:16:17,990
I can feel it, we're falling
through Space, you and me.

163
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:21,458
Clinging to the skin of this tiny
little world, and if we let go...

164
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:29,849
That's who I am.
Now forget me, Rose Tyler.

165
00:16:29,940 --> 00:16:32,295
Go home.

166
00:17:01,020 --> 00:17:03,534
STRANGE MACHINE-LIKE NOISE

167
00:17:32,020 --> 00:17:34,329
H... hey, here's my woman! Kit off.

168
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:38,538
Oh, shut up. Coffee?
Yeah, only if you wash the mug.

169
00:17:38,620 --> 00:17:42,579
I don't mean rinse, I mean wash.
Can I use your computer?

170
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:46,130
Yeah, any excuse
to get in the bedroom.

171
00:17:46,220 --> 00:17:49,980
Don't read my e-mails!

172
00:18:29,260 --> 00:18:31,410
You're not coming in.

173
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:34,936
He's safe, he's got a wife and kids.

174
00:18:35,020 --> 00:18:40,140
Who told you that? He did!
That's exactly what an internet
lunatic murderer would say.

175
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:06,573
Um, hello, I've come to see Clive.
We've been e-mailing.

176
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:10,960
Dad! It's one of your nutters.

177
00:19:12,740 --> 00:19:16,779
Sorry, hello! You must be Rose.
I'm Clive. Obviously.

178
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:21,251
I'd better tell you - my boyfriend's
in the car, in case you kill me!

179
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:25,299
No, good point! No murders!
Who is it?

180
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:30,898
It's to do with the Doctor,
she's been reading the website.
Please come through, I'm in the shed.

181
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:36,769
She? She's read a website
about the Doctor, she's a she?

182
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:45,219
This is quite sensitive, I couldn't
just send it. People might intercept.

183
00:19:45,300 --> 00:19:49,540
If you know what I mean.
If you dig deep enough

184
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:53,418
and keep a lively mind, this Doctor
keeps cropping up all over the place.

185
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:57,812
Political diaries, conspiracy
theories, even ghost stories.

186
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:03,540
No first name, no last name,
just the Doctor. Always the Doctor.

187
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:07,895
The title seems to be passed from
father to son, like an inheritance.

188
00:20:07,980 --> 00:20:10,733
That's your Doctor there, isn't it?

189
00:20:10,820 --> 00:20:14,654
Yeah. I tracked it down to the
Washington Public Archive, last year.

190
00:20:14,740 --> 00:20:19,177
The online photo's enhanced,
but if we look at the original...

191
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:35,772
November 22nd 1963, the assassination
of President Kennedy. See.

192
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:39,656
Must be his father.

193
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:42,950
Going further back...

194
00:20:42,180 --> 00:20:44,216
April 1912,

195
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:49,328
this is a photograph of the Daniels
family of Southampton, and friend...

196
00:20:49,420 --> 00:20:53,538
Taken the day before they were due to
go to the new world. On the Titanic.

197
00:20:53,620 --> 00:20:57,659
But for some unknown reason, they
cancelled the trip, and survived.

198
00:20:57,740 --> 00:21:00,413
And here we are...

199
00:21:00,500 --> 00:21:03,298
1883, another Doctor.

200
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:07,214
Look, the same lineage,
he's identical...

201
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:12,294
This one washed up on the Sumatran
coast, the night Krakatoa exploded.

202
00:21:12,380 --> 00:21:15,770
The Doctor is a legend,
woven throughout history.

203
00:21:15,860 --> 00:21:17,816
When disaster comes, he's there.

204
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:22,928
He brings the storm in his wake,
and has one constant companion.
Who's that?

205
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:24,931
Death.

206
00:21:46,340 --> 00:21:50,413
If the Doctor's back,
if you've seen him, Rose,

207
00:21:50,500 --> 00:21:52,934
one thing's for certain.

208
00:21:53,020 --> 00:21:55,250
We're all in danger.

209
00:22:29,260 --> 00:22:34,857
Come on then. If he singled you out,
if the Doctor's making house calls...

210
00:22:37,340 --> 00:22:39,251
..then God help you.

211
00:22:50,340 --> 00:22:53,332
BIN ROARS

212
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:22,173
BIN BURPS
But who is he?

213
00:23:22,260 --> 00:23:24,171
Who d'you think he is?

214
00:23:24,260 --> 00:23:26,899
I think he's the same man.

215
00:23:26,980 --> 00:23:33,897
I think he's immortal. I think
he's an alien from another world.

216
00:23:35,380 --> 00:23:38,531
All right, he's a nutter.
Off his head.

217
00:23:38,620 --> 00:23:41,976
Complete online conspiracy freak,
you win!

218
00:23:42,060 --> 00:23:44,176
So, what are we going to do tonight?

219
00:23:44,260 --> 00:23:46,820
I fancy a pizza.

220
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:48,811
Pizza! Puh-puh-puh.

221
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:51,209
Pizza! Or Chinese.

222
00:23:51,300 --> 00:23:53,495
Pizzaaaaaaaa!

223
00:24:02,340 --> 00:24:04,615
Should I try the hospital?

224
00:24:04,700 --> 00:24:08,409
Suki said they had jobs going
in the canteen.

225
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:12,413
Is that it then, dishing out chips?

226
00:24:12,500 --> 00:24:14,809
I could do A-levels. I dunno.

227
00:24:14,900 --> 00:24:20,611
It's all Jimmy Stones's fault.
I only left school cos of him
and look where he ended up.

228
00:24:20,700 --> 00:24:22,452
What do you think?

229
00:24:22,540 --> 00:24:24,371
So where did you meet this Doctor?

230
00:24:24,460 --> 00:24:26,815
Oh, sorry, was I talking about me?

231
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:28,891
I reckon it started at the shop,
am I right?

232
00:24:28,980 --> 00:24:31,369
Was he something to do with that?
No.

233
00:24:31,460 --> 00:24:33,690
Come on.

234
00:24:33,780 --> 00:24:35,975
Sort of.

235
00:24:36,060 --> 00:24:40,530
What was he doing there? I'm not
going on about it, really I'm not.

236
00:24:40,140 --> 00:24:42,415
Cos I know it sounds daft,

237
00:24:42,500 --> 00:24:44,809
but I don't think he's safe.

238
00:24:44,900 --> 00:24:47,733
He's dangerous. You can trust me,
sweetheart.

239
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:50,698
HIS VOICE IS ROBOTIC AT TURNS
Babe, darling, sugar...

240
00:24:50,780 --> 00:24:56,930
You can tell me anything.
Tell me about the Doctor and what
he's planning. I can help you, Rose.

241
00:24:56,180 --> 00:25:00,139
That's all I want, sweetheart,
darling, babe, sugar sweetheart.

242
00:25:00,220 --> 00:25:04,990
What are you doing that for?
Champagne. We didn't order any.

243
00:25:04,180 --> 00:25:06,899
Where's the Doctor?
Madam, your champagne.

244
00:25:06,980 --> 00:25:10,575
It's not ours.
Mickey, what is it, what's wrong?

245
00:25:10,660 --> 00:25:13,940
I need know out how much he knows,
so where is he?

246
00:25:13,180 --> 00:25:16,331
Doesn't anybody want this champagne?
Look, we didn't order...

247
00:25:17,500 --> 00:25:21,459
Ah, gotcha. Don't mind me.
I'm just toasting the happy couple.

248
00:25:21,540 --> 00:25:23,735
On the house!

249
00:25:29,660 --> 00:25:31,730
Anyway!

250
00:25:42,940 --> 00:25:46,410
Don't think that's gonna stop me.

251
00:25:48,580 --> 00:25:50,730
Everyone, out, now!

252
00:25:54,100 --> 00:25:57,376
Get out, get out, get out!

253
00:26:18,020 --> 00:26:20,614
Open the gate! Use that tube thing!

254
00:26:20,700 --> 00:26:22,691
Sonic screwdriver. Use it!

255
00:26:22,780 --> 00:26:26,110
Nah, tell you what, let's go in here.

256
00:26:31,060 --> 00:26:33,255
You can't hide in a wooden box!

257
00:26:37,780 --> 00:26:39,771
He's gonna get us!

258
00:26:41,060 --> 00:26:42,971
Doctor!

259
00:27:07,780 --> 00:27:09,611
It's gonna follow us.

260
00:27:09,700 --> 00:27:13,693
The assembled hordes of Genghis Khan
couldn't get through that door.

261
00:27:13,780 --> 00:27:17,568
Believe me, they've tried!
Now, shut up a minute.

262
00:27:23,420 --> 00:27:29,170
You see, the arm was too simple,
but a head's perfect.

263
00:27:29,100 --> 00:27:34,128
I can use it to trace the signal
back to the original source.

264
00:27:34,220 --> 00:27:36,609
Right. Where d'you want to start?

265
00:27:36,700 --> 00:27:39,931
Um... The inside's bigger
than the outside.

266
00:27:40,020 --> 00:27:42,110
Yes. It's... alien.

267
00:27:42,100 --> 00:27:46,130
Yep... Are you alien?

268
00:27:46,100 --> 00:27:48,773
Yes.

269
00:27:48,860 --> 00:27:50,578
Is that all right? Yeah.

270
00:27:50,660 --> 00:27:52,571
It's called the Tardis, this thing.

271
00:27:52,660 --> 00:27:56,653
T-A-R-D-I-S, that's Time And
Relative Dimension In Space.

272
00:27:57,780 --> 00:27:59,816
That's OK. Culture shock.

273
00:27:59,900 --> 00:28:03,813
Happens to the best of us.
Did they kill him? Mickey?

274
00:28:03,900 --> 00:28:05,811
Did they kill Mickey? Is he dead?

275
00:28:05,900 --> 00:28:08,460
Oh, I didn't think of that.

276
00:28:08,540 --> 00:28:14,251
He's my boyfriend! You pulled off
his head, they copied him,
and you didn't even think?

277
00:28:14,340 --> 00:28:16,649
Now you're just gonna let him melt.
Melt?!

278
00:28:18,980 --> 00:28:22,256
Aw, no, no, no, NO!

279
00:28:22,340 --> 00:28:26,936
What are you doing? Following
the signal. It's fading!

280
00:28:28,380 --> 00:28:30,655
No, no, no, no, no, no, NO!

281
00:28:32,860 --> 00:28:35,135
Almost there, almost there...

282
00:28:35,220 --> 00:28:37,336
Here we go!

283
00:28:39,460 --> 00:28:43,373
You can't go out there.
It's not safe!

284
00:28:46,260 --> 00:28:49,172
I lost the signal. I got so close.

285
00:28:50,580 --> 00:28:53,219
We've moved. Does it fly?

286
00:28:53,300 --> 00:28:55,530
It disappears there
and reappears here.

287
00:28:55,620 --> 00:29:00,570
But if we're... somewhere else, that
headless thing's still on the loose.

288
00:29:00,140 --> 00:29:05,737
Melted with the head.
Are you gonna witter on all night?
I'll have to tell his mother.

289
00:29:06,820 --> 00:29:12,770
Mickey. I'll have to tell his
mother he's dead, and you just
went and forgot him. Again!

290
00:29:12,860 --> 00:29:14,737
You were right. You are alien.

291
00:29:14,820 --> 00:29:17,732
If I did forget some kid called
Mickey. He's not a kid!

292
00:29:17,820 --> 00:29:21,449
..It's because I'm trying to save
every stupid ape blundering about

293
00:29:21,540 --> 00:29:25,550
on this planet, all right?
All right?! Yes, it is!

294
00:29:25,140 --> 00:29:28,735
If you are an alien, why do you
sound like you're from the north?

295
00:29:28,820 --> 00:29:30,731
Lots of planets have a north!

296
00:29:31,780 --> 00:29:34,658
..What's a police public call box?

297
00:29:37,260 --> 00:29:41,731
It's a telephone box,
from the 1950s. It's a disguise.

298
00:29:42,700 --> 00:29:46,693
OK. And, this, this living plastic,
what's it got against us?

299
00:29:46,780 --> 00:29:50,739
Nothing. It loves you. You've got a
good planet, lots of smoke and oil,

300
00:29:50,820 --> 00:29:55,769
plenty of toxins and dioxins,
perfect. Just what
the Nestene Consciousness needs.

301
00:29:55,860 --> 00:29:59,409
Its food stock was destroyed in
the war, its protein planets rotted.

302
00:29:59,500 --> 00:30:04,960
So. Earth. Dinner.
Any way of stopping it? Antiplastic.

303
00:30:04,180 --> 00:30:05,772
Antiplastic? Antiplastic!

304
00:30:05,860 --> 00:30:07,816
But first, I've got to find it.

305
00:30:07,900 --> 00:30:10,937
How can you hide something that big
in a city this small?

306
00:30:11,020 --> 00:30:12,976
Hide what? A transmitter.

307
00:30:13,060 --> 00:30:16,291
The Consciousness
is controlling all plastic,

308
00:30:16,380 --> 00:30:20,259
a transmitter boosts the signal. What
does it look like? A transmitter!

309
00:30:20,340 --> 00:30:23,130
Round and massive -
in the middle of London.

310
00:30:23,100 --> 00:30:27,590
A huge, metal, circular structure,
like a dish, like a wheel, radial,

311
00:30:27,140 --> 00:30:31,292
close to where we're standing,
it must be completely invisible.

312
00:30:31,380 --> 00:30:32,893
What?

313
00:30:34,380 --> 00:30:36,610
What?

314
00:30:37,900 --> 00:30:40,414
What is it? What?

315
00:30:42,860 --> 00:30:44,896
Oh.

316
00:30:46,780 --> 00:30:49,248
Fantastic!

317
00:31:08,500 --> 00:31:13,290
Think. Plastic. Everywhere, every
artificial thing waiting to be alive.

318
00:31:13,380 --> 00:31:16,690
The shop window dummies,
phones, wires, cables.

319
00:31:16,780 --> 00:31:19,977
The breast implants.
Still, we've found the transmitter.

320
00:31:20,060 --> 00:31:23,257
The Consciousness must be
somewhere underneath.

321
00:31:24,900 --> 00:31:27,778
What about down here?

322
00:31:29,580 --> 00:31:31,730
Looks good to me.

323
00:32:13,820 --> 00:32:15,890
The Nestene Consciousness.

324
00:32:15,980 --> 00:32:19,859
That's it, inside the vat,
a living plastic creature.

325
00:32:19,940 --> 00:32:26,618
Well, tip in your antiplastic
and let's go. I'm not here to kill
it. I've got to give it a chance.

326
00:32:30,700 --> 00:32:36,130
I seek audience with the Nestene
Consciousness under peaceful contract

327
00:32:36,100 --> 00:32:40,590
according to Convention 15
of the Shadow Proclamation.

328
00:32:42,220 --> 00:32:45,929
Thank you. If I might have
permission to approach.

329
00:32:47,300 --> 00:32:50,190
Oh, my God.

330
00:32:51,460 --> 00:32:54,418
Mickey! It's me! It's OK.

331
00:32:54,500 --> 00:32:57,731
It's all right. Shhh.
That thing, down there...

332
00:32:57,820 --> 00:33:00,778
The liquid, it can talk!
Oh, you're stinking!

333
00:33:00,860 --> 00:33:02,737
Doctor, they kept him alive!

334
00:33:02,820 --> 00:33:06,733
Yeah, that was always a possibility -
keep him alive to maintain the copy.

335
00:33:06,820 --> 00:33:11,180
You knew that and never said?! Can
we keep domestics outside, thank you!

336
00:33:22,820 --> 00:33:25,812
Am I addressing the Consciousness?

337
00:33:25,900 --> 00:33:28,289
Thank you. If I might observe,

338
00:33:28,380 --> 00:33:32,817
you infiltrated this civilisation
by means of warp, shunt technology.

339
00:33:32,900 --> 00:33:36,449
So, may I suggest, with greatest
respect, that you shunt off?!

340
00:33:36,540 --> 00:33:41,295
Oh, don't give me that! It's an
invasion, plain and simple.

341
00:33:41,380 --> 00:33:43,689
Don't talk
about constitutional rights.

342
00:33:45,900 --> 00:33:48,892
I AM TALKING!

343
00:33:48,980 --> 00:33:51,494
This planet is just starting.

344
00:33:51,580 --> 00:33:56,859
These stupid, little people
have just learnt how to walk.
They are capable of so much more.

345
00:33:56,940 --> 00:34:01,616
I'm asking you, on their behalf.
Please, just go. Doctor!

346
00:34:07,260 --> 00:34:10,730
That was just insurance!
I wasn't gonna use it.

347
00:34:12,500 --> 00:34:17,960
I was not attacking you. I'm here to
help. I'm not your enemy, I swear.

348
00:34:19,460 --> 00:34:22,213
What do you mean?

349
00:34:22,300 --> 00:34:24,894
No! Honestly, no...

350
00:34:24,980 --> 00:34:27,540
Yes, that's my ship.

351
00:34:28,740 --> 00:34:30,731
That's not true!

352
00:34:30,820 --> 00:34:34,779
I should know, I was there. I fought
in the war. It wasn't my fault.

353
00:34:34,860 --> 00:34:38,170
I couldn't save your world.
I couldn't save any of them.

354
00:34:40,260 --> 00:34:42,120
What's it doing? It's the Tardis.

355
00:34:42,100 --> 00:34:45,979
The Nestene's identified it as
superior technology. It's terrified!

356
00:34:46,060 --> 00:34:48,699
It's going to the final base.

357
00:34:48,780 --> 00:34:53,580
It's starting the invasion...
Get out, Rose! Just leg it!

358
00:34:54,300 --> 00:34:57,417
Mum? Oh, there you are.
I was gonna phone.

359
00:34:57,500 --> 00:35:02,369
You CAN get compensation. I've got
this document thing off the police.
Don't thank me!

360
00:35:02,460 --> 00:35:05,990
Where are you, Mum? I'm in town.

361
00:35:05,180 --> 00:35:07,296
Look, go! Just go home right now.

362
00:35:07,380 --> 00:35:12,579
Darling, you're breaking up.
I'm just gonna do a bit shopping.
I'll see you later, ta-ra.

363
00:35:12,660 --> 00:35:14,332
Mum? Mum?

364
00:35:19,860 --> 00:35:25,930
It's the activation signal!
It's transmitting.

365
00:35:29,260 --> 00:35:31,410
It's the end of the world.

366
00:35:39,380 --> 00:35:42,611
There's no point in a spreadsheet
if you spend summer money in winter.

367
00:35:42,700 --> 00:35:47,569
My God! I thought they were dummies!
I nearly had a heart attack.

368
00:36:12,820 --> 00:36:17,416
It's true. Everything I've read.
All those stories, it's all true.

369
00:36:25,180 --> 00:36:27,933
Get out, Rose! Just get out!

370
00:36:28,020 --> 00:36:30,739
RUN! The stairs have gone.

371
00:36:35,740 --> 00:36:38,379
I haven't got a key...

372
00:36:40,020 --> 00:36:41,976
We're gonna die!

373
00:38:00,900 --> 00:38:03,334
Leave him!

374
00:38:08,780 --> 00:38:11,294
There's nothing you can do!

375
00:38:11,380 --> 00:38:13,450
I've got no A-levels,

376
00:38:13,540 --> 00:38:15,690
no job.

377
00:38:15,780 --> 00:38:17,896
No future.

378
00:38:17,980 --> 00:38:20,813
But I'll tell you what I have got.

379
00:38:20,900 --> 00:38:23,937
Jericho Street Junior School
Under-7s gymnastic team.

380
00:38:24,020 --> 00:38:26,900
I got the bronze!

381
00:38:39,020 --> 00:38:41,560
Rose!

382
00:38:44,100 --> 00:38:46,330
Now we're in trouble!

383
00:40:20,820 --> 00:40:23,778
Rose, don't go out of the house!

384
00:40:23,860 --> 00:40:27,773
'Lt's not safe. There are these
things, they were shooting and... '

385
00:40:27,860 --> 00:40:30,420
Hello?

386
00:40:32,260 --> 00:40:35,809
Fat lot of good you were!

387
00:40:38,860 --> 00:40:42,570
Nestene Consciousness? Easy!

388
00:40:42,140 --> 00:40:46,990
You were useless! You'd be dead if
it wasn't for me. Yes, I would.

389
00:40:46,180 --> 00:40:49,297
..Thank you. Right, then!

390
00:40:49,380 --> 00:40:51,336
I'll be off.

391
00:40:51,420 --> 00:40:53,376
Unless... I dunno.

392
00:40:53,460 --> 00:40:55,371
You could come with me.

393
00:40:55,460 --> 00:41:01,490
This box isn't just a London hopper,
you know. It goes anywhere
in the universe. Free of charge.

394
00:41:01,580 --> 00:41:03,855
Don't! He's an alien, he's a thing.

395
00:41:03,940 --> 00:41:06,135
He's not invited.

396
00:41:06,220 --> 00:41:09,132
What d'you think?

397
00:41:09,220 --> 00:41:11,176
You could... stay here.

398
00:41:11,260 --> 00:41:15,856
Fill your life with work and food and
sleep, or you could go... anywhere.

399
00:41:15,940 --> 00:41:19,171
Is it always this dangerous? Yeah.

400
00:41:21,260 --> 00:41:23,251
Yeah... I can't.

401
00:41:23,340 --> 00:41:29,256
I've got to go and find my mum
and someone's got to look
after this stupid lump. So...

402
00:41:31,580 --> 00:41:34,299
OK. See you around.

403
00:42:06,700 --> 00:42:08,691
Come on, let's go.

404
00:42:27,660 --> 00:42:32,211
By the way, did I mention
it also travels in time?

405
00:42:35,620 --> 00:42:38,976
Thanks. Thanks for what?

406
00:42:39,060 --> 00:42:41,779
Exactly.

407
00:42:51,780 --> 00:42:55,560
This is the year five billion,

408
00:42:55,140 --> 00:42:57,290
and this is the day... Hold on...

409
00:42:58,900 --> 00:43:02,176
Welcome to the end of the world.

410
00:43:02,260 --> 00:43:06,253
Who the hell are you? Ooh,
I'm The Doctor this is Rose Tyler.

411
00:43:06,340 --> 00:43:08,296
She's my plus one, is that all right?

412
00:43:08,380 --> 00:43:14,410
Representing the Forest of Cheam,
we have Trees, the Moxx of Balhoon,

413
00:43:14,500 --> 00:43:20,655
the Face of Boe, the last human -
the Lady Cassandra O'Brien.

414
00:43:20,740 --> 00:43:24,255
Oh, now, don't stare,
look how thin I am.

415
00:43:26,700 --> 00:43:28,190
That's not supposed to happen.
